  user_input {
    user_response: "Role: You are an expert Full-Stack Software Engineer and Accessibility (AAC) UX Architect.\n\nGoal: Build a functional Single-Page Web Application (SPA) for a Context-Adaptive Communication Board using free ARASAC pictograms (Polish language). \n\nTechnical & Architectural Rules:\n1. Tech Stack: Single-file HTML/JavaScript (ES6) with Tailwind CSS via CDN for fast prototyping and preview. No build steps required.\n2. Pictogram Source: Use official ARASAC API and static assets:\n   - Search Endpoint: `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/pl/search/{query}`\n   - Static Image URL: `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/{id}/{id}_500.png`\n3. Audio / Offline constraints: Do NOT include Text-To-Speech (TTS) or Offline/ServiceWorker logic. This is an ONLINE-ONLY, SILENT (visual-only) MVP.\n\nApplication Layout Structure:\n1. Top Section - Sentence Bar (Pasekw wypowiedzi):\n   - Array of selected pictogram tiles.\n   - Clear button (\"Wyczy\305\233\304\207\") and Backspace button (\"Usu\305\204 ostatni\").\n   - \"Full Screen View\" (\"Powi\304\231ksz\") modal/overlay button to show the composed sentence in large scale on the screen for visual communication.\n2. Core Vocabulary Grid (70% main area - Left/Top):\n   - Fixed, static grid of essential core words (\"ja\", \"chc\304\231\", \"nie\", \"lubi\304\231\", \"to\", \"gdzie\", \"stop\", \"wi\304\231cej\").\n   - These MUST NOT change position when context changes to preserve muscle memory.\n   - Map these core words to static ARASAC Pictogram IDs.\n3. Dynamic Context Panel (30% secondary area - Right/Bottom):\n   - Adapts based on context triggers:\n     a) Manual Selectors: Quick toggle buttons for contexts (\"Dom\", \"Szko\305\202a\", \"Park\", \"Jedzenie\").\n     b) Time Context: Reads system JS Date() to favor Morning vs Evening vocabulary.\n     c) Sequential Prediction: Selecting a verb (e.g., \"chc\304\231\") automatically loads \"Nouns/Objects\" in the dynamic panel.\n     d) Geolocation API: Option button to \"Use my location\" using `navigator.geolocation` to infer current place.\n\nFunctional Capabilities:\n- Interactive pictograms: Clicking any card adds it to the Sentence Bar.\n- Fetching: Dynamic panel must fetch pictogram IDs from ARASAC API dynamically based on context tags if not hardcoded.\n- Design: Clean, high-contrast UI suitable for users with cognitive or visual needs.\n\nDeliverable:\nProvide the full, standalone, robust HTML/JS/CSS code ready to run directly in any browser. Include comments explaining how ARASAC API fetching and the context engine work."
    items {
      text: "Role: You are an expert Full-Stack Software Engineer and Accessibility (AAC) UX Architect.\n\nGoal: Build a functional Single-Page Web Application (SPA) for a Context-Adaptive Communication Board using free ARASAC pictograms (Polish language). \n\nTechnical & Architectural Rules:\n1. Tech Stack: Single-file HTML/JavaScript (ES6) with Tailwind CSS via CDN for fast prototyping and preview. No build steps required.\n2. Pictogram Source: Use official ARASAC API and static assets:\n   - Search Endpoint: `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/pl/search/{query}`\n   - Static Image URL: `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/{id}/{id}_500.png`\n3. Audio / Offline constraints: Do NOT include Text-To-Speech (TTS) or Offline/ServiceWorker logic. This is an ONLINE-ONLY, SILENT (visual-only) MVP.\n\nApplication Layout Structure:\n1. Top Section - Sentence Bar (Pasekw wypowiedzi):\n   - Array of selected pictogram tiles.\n   - Clear button (\"Wyczy\305\233\304\207\") and Backspace button (\"Usu\305\204 ostatni\").\n   - \"Full Screen View\" (\"Powi\304\231ksz\") modal/overlay button to show the composed sentence in large scale on the screen for visual communication.\n2. Core Vocabulary Grid (70% main area - Left/Top):\n   - Fixed, static grid of essential core words (\"ja\", \"chc\304\231\", \"nie\", \"lubi\304\231\", \"to\", \"gdzie\", \"stop\", \"wi\304\231cej\").\n   - These MUST NOT change position when context changes to preserve muscle memory.\n   - Map these core words to static ARASAC Pictogram IDs.\n3. Dynamic Context Panel (30% secondary area - Right/Bottom):\n   - Adapts based on context triggers:\n     a) Manual Selectors: Quick toggle buttons for contexts (\"Dom\", \"Szko\305\202a\", \"Park\", \"Jedzenie\").\n     b) Time Context: Reads system JS Date() to favor Morning vs Evening vocabulary.\n     c) Sequential Prediction: Selecting a verb (e.g., \"chc\304\231\") automatically loads \"Nouns/Objects\" in the dynamic panel.\n     d) Geolocation API: Option button to \"Use my location\" using `navigator.geolocation` to infer current place.\n\nFunctional Capabilities:\n- Interactive pictograms: Clicking any card adds it to the Sentence Bar.\n- Fetching: Dynamic panel must fetch pictogram IDs from ARASAC API dynamically based on context tags if not hardcoded.\n- Design: Clean, high-contrast UI suitable for users with cognitive or visual needs.\n\nDeliverable:\nProvide the full, standalone, robust HTML/JS/CSS code ready to run directly in any browser. Include comments explaining how ARASAC API fetching and the context engine work."
    }
  }
}
