  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing AAC Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the requirements for a Context-Adaptive Communication Board specifically in Polish, utilizing ARASAAC pictograms. I\'m taking the initial steps of defining the layout. The aim is to create an intuitive and adaptive AAC experience.\n\n\n**Defining Sentence Bar Features**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the specific features for the sentence bar. I\'m prioritizing the inclusion of a clear button, backspace, and a full-screen view for the composed message. I am also considering adding helpful extra tools to further improve the user\'s experience with the board. The goal is easy and intuitive access.\n\n\n**Mapping Core Words Reliably**\n\nI am now deep diving into the critical aspect of color-coding and mapping core words to ARASAAC pictogram IDs to create a highly functional vocabulary. I\'ve compiled a list of key words and am cross-referencing to ensure I have reliable pictogram IDs as a foundation. For example, I have already checked and confirmed IDs for \"ja\", \"chc\304\231\", \"nie\", \"lubi\304\231\", \"to\", \"gdzie\", \"stop\", \"wi\304\231cej\", \"tak\", \"prosz\304\231\", \"dzi\304\231kuj\304\231\", \"pomoc\", \"je\305\233\304\207\", and others.\n\n\n**Confirming Core Vocabulary**\n\nI\'m now verifying pictogram IDs for more words to further enrich the board\'s vocabulary. Specifically, I\'ve confirmed IDs for \"pi\304\207\", \"i\305\233\304\207\", \"toaleta\", \"to\", \"dobrze\", and \"\305\272le\" in both the ARASAAC database and a secondary reference to ensure accuracy. I\'m also looking into how to access ARASAAC images using their endpoints to display them on the board.\n\n**Constructing Dynamic Contexts**\n\nI\'m in the process of designing a dynamic context panel. I\'m aiming for it to adapt based on manual selectors (home, school, emotions, etc.) and time of day, pulling from the system\'s `Date()` to favour morning or evening words. I\'m determining which contexts to prioritize.\n\n\n**Implementing Contextual Prediction**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the dynamic context panel to provide sequential prediction. Based on the date, the panel will dynamically respond to selected verbs, such as \"chc\304\231\", \"lubi\304\231\", or \"je\305\233\304\207\", and suggest appropriate nouns or objects. I will use the established categories and ARASAAC pictograms. The goal is an intuitive and responsive communication experience. I am currently evaluating verb-noun associations to enhance context and improve the suggestion accuracy.\n\n\n**Adding Location Integration**\n\nI am now integrating location services. Specifically, after the user clicks \"i\305\233\304\207\", I will suggest places like \"dom\", \"park,\" or \"szko\305\202a\" and display a clear indicator that the suggestions are based on word prediction. There will also be a button to get the user\'s location via geolocation, which automatically selects the nearest context. I will ensure clear user feedback and fallback mechanisms. I\'m also planning to build a dynamic ARASAAC fetching and search engine.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Pictogram Loading**\n\nI\'m now focusing on pre-verifying ARASAAC IDs so that, even if the API network request is delayed, the application renders instant, zero-latency pictograms.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 730654784
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
