    thinking: "**Defining Application Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m now delving into the architectural design. I\'m starting by meticulously outlining the data structures, specifically focusing on the `Pictogram` type within `src/types.ts`. This involves defining the specific properties for each pictogram, including its ID, associated word, potential category, Fitzgerald color, and flags for customization and associated tags.\n\n\n**Categorizing Core Vocabulary**\n\nI\'m now determining context and time-of-day categories, mapping the core vocabulary. This builds on the `FitzgeraldCategory` concept, expanding it to include context, and also the time of day the pictogram is used. The goal is to define specific use cases for the core 12-20 words, each with a fixed ID from ARASAC.\n\n\n**Mapping Core Vocabulary**\n\nI am now adding the core vocabulary, noting that these items NEVER shift position to preserve motor memory. I\'m focusing on their ARASAC IDs, and associated metadata to create the context preset data, specifically targeting the Polish core vocabulary. I\'ve got \"ja\", \"ty\", \"chc\304\231\", \"nie\", \"tak\", \"lubi\304\231\", \"to\", \"gdzie\", \"stop\", \"wi\304\231cej\", \"pomoc\", \"prosz\304\231\", \"dzi\304\231kuj\304\231\", \"je\305\233\304\207\", \"pi\304\207\", \"i\305\233\304\207\", \"toaleta\", and \"dobrze\" to add.\n\n\n**Expanding Vocabulary Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the Polish vocabulary to include additional words beyond the core set. I\'ve categorized them thematically, covering home items like \"st\303\263\305\202\" and \"fotel\", school supplies like \"nauczyciel\" and \"ksi\304\205\305\274ka\", and outdoor elements like \"drzewo\" and \"plac zabaw\". The goal is to provide a broader semantic range. I\'m also including foods, and finally, emotions.\n\n\n**Adding More Vocabulary**\n\nI am now adding several more words, focusing on additional Polish vocabulary. I\'ve included categories for \"Miejsca\" (places), such as \"dom\" and \"szko\305\202a\", \"Zabawa\" (play & hobbies) with items like \"gra\" and \"klocki\", and \"Zdrowie\" (health & hygiene), including terms like \"lekarz\" and \"boli\". I am also beginning to integrate concepts for auto-categorization based on the time of day, and starting to map out sequential logic based on verb and trigger word inputs.\n\n\n**Implementing Predictive Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing predictive text functionality. I\'m focusing on how verbs trigger specific vocabulary categories to appear as suggestions. For instance, \"chc\304\231\" triggers Food and Objects, while \"je\305\233\304\207\" and \"pi\304\207\" lead to Food and Beverage items, respectively. The system will display a predictive banner to prompt the user.\n\n\n**Defining API and UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the backend ARASAC API with the frontend components. I\'m focusing on how the search endpoint `/search/${encodeURIComponent(query)}` returns pictogram data, and how I\'ll use it with the static image URL generator `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/${id}/${id}_500.png`. I\'m also implementing robust error handling and fallback mechanisms for API requests. Furthermore, I\'m working on the `SentenceBar.tsx`, `CoreGrid.tsx`, and `ContextPanel.tsx` components for an effective UI. I will also incorporate the Geolocation Service to determine context.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI component design and structure, creating new files in `/src/`. I\'m focusing on modularity, starting with `PictogramCard.tsx` for accessible pictogram cards, integrating ARASAC images, Polish labels, and Fitzgerald color coding. I\'m also planning the `FullScreenSentenceModal.tsx` for immersive presentations, and `SettingsBar.tsx` for customization. I will also incorporate the Geolocation Service to determine context. I\'ll need to create `src/types.ts`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 798301563
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
