    thinking: "**Constructing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI components! My current focus is building out `PictogramCard.tsx`. It will feature a highly accessible tile displaying ARASAC images, with a fallback icon for loading failures. AAC standards are my guide as I determine the label placement, either above or below the image.\n\n\n**Refining UI Interactivity**\n\nI\'m now implementing the interactive features for the UI components. I\'ve designed a click handler for the `PictogramCard` that adds tiles to the sentence bar. High contrast mode support is on the list, as are the focus rings and touch responses, focusing on the accessibility standards. I am currently adding the quick action badge, and I\'m developing the actions for the sentence bar buttons.\n\n\n**Designing Contextual Panels**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the context panel, which will be secondary and collapsible. This panel will include category selection tabs such as \"Dom\", \"Szko\305\202a\", and \"Jedzenie\", and a time-based trigger with manual override. I\'m planning to add a geolocation trigger and a sequential prediction indicator, enhancing the user experience. I\'m also including a live search input for ARASAC pictograms. I\'m simultaneously prototyping a fullscreen modal for sentence display.\n\n\n"
