  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying All Requirements**\n\nI\'ve successfully compiled the applet on the initial attempt! Now, I am meticulously double-checking every requirement from the prompt to guarantee complete satisfaction. Specifically, I\'m focusing on confirming the chosen tech stack (React + Vite + Tailwind CSS for a single-page web app within a container with full interactivity), and the pictogram source (official ARAS).\n\n\n**Analyzing App Features**\n\nI\'ve completed the preliminary checks and am now dissecting the requested features. The design is solidified: a visual-only MVP. I\'m focusing on the app\'s structure: a sentence bar, a core vocabulary grid, and a dynamic context panel. I am especially considering how to arrange the context panels: manual selectors, time-sensitive vocabulary, and sequential prediction.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built the **Context-Adaptive AAC Communication Board (Tablica Komunikacyjna AAC)** using official Polish ARASAC pictograms.\n\n### Key Features & Design Architecture:\n- **Top Section \342\200\224 Sentence Bar (Pasek wypowiedzi)**:\n  - Displays selected pictogram cards in chronological order with Polish text labels.\n  - Controls include **Wyczy\305\233\304\207** (clear all), **Usu\305\204 ostatni** (backspace), **Kopiuj** (copy text), and **Powi\304\231ksz** (fullscreen visual display mode).\n  - Tapping individual tiles in the bar removes them instantly.\n\n- **Core Vocabulary Grid (70% Area \342\200\224 Fixed Layout)**:\n  - Fixed, static grid featuring essential core words (*ja, chc\304\231, nie, lubi\304\231, to, gdzie, stop, wi\304\231cej, tak, prosz\304\231, dzi\304\231kuj\304\231, pomoc, je\305\233\304\207, pi\304\207, i\305\233\304\207, toaleta*).\n  - Maintains static card positions across context changes to preserve muscle memory for non-verbal users.\n  - Color-coded using the international **Fitzgerald Key** standard (pronouns in yellow/gold, verbs in green, nouns in orange, descriptors in blue, courtesy in pink, questions in purple, negation/stop in red).\n\n- **Dynamic Context Panel (30% Area \342\200\224 Adaptive Section)**:\n  - **Manual Context Selectors**: Quick tabs for *Dom, Szko\305\202a, Park, Jedzenie, Emocje, Miejsca, Zabawa, Zdrowie*.\n  - **Time-of-Day Context**: Automatically reads system `Date()` to surface morning (*Rano*), afternoon (*Popo\305\202udnie*), or evening/night (*Wiecz\303\263r*) vocabulary with manual override options.\n  - **Sequential Prediction**: Selecting a verb (*chc\304\231, je\305\233\304\207, pi\304\207, i\305\233\304\207, lubi\304\231, gdzie, boli*) automatically loads relevant noun/object complements in the dynamic panel.\n  - **Geolocation API**: \"Moja Lokalizacja\" button uses `navigator.geolocation` to infer current place context.\n  - **Real-Time ARASAC Search Engine**: Input box allowing real-time searches against `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/pl/search/{query}`.\n\n- **Fullscreen Visual Presentation Modal (Powi\304\231ksz)**:\n  - High-impact overlay displaying composed sentences in large format for easy communication across a room or table.\n\n- **Accessibility & Contrast**:\n  - High Contrast mode toggle (*Wysoki Kontrast*), color key legend drawer, and touch-optimized card sizes."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 372772973
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
