      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHHeifdy_FJpYxXAhtkDspyYtxfch_pLzsCzSYPw_8MVyVvPB_JGwRLh5LgIxRh8zadhoJRg7WBq6BQYkoqtYOVFBiYHMg9Xpjrq2Bba_bHUsasPrVyqS5Ms6qpnUyTmful1fxo9LsKQD5HkBIuqQo1Kh4dHZXo-kBzrzb598bzudajwFlST6nABexpK-4D5lK0IEnQdg=="
      title: "arasaac.org"
    }
    summary: "ARASAAC provides an API for accessing its pictograms, which is utilized by various applications such as Asterics AAC for real-time pictogram search and customization options[1].\n\nWhile a direct public CDN API domain for raw pictogram images isn\'t explicitly stated in the search results, several GitHub repositories and discussions point to the existence and use of an ARASAAC API:\n*   The `arasaac-admin` GitHub repository mentions an API developed with Node.js for managing pictograms, materials, and users[2].\n*   Another repository, `agfaya/arasaac-api`, seems to be a related project, although it suggests decompressing a `pictograms.rar` file locally for use[3]. This might indicate a way to get the raw files, but not necessarily a CDN.\n*   The official ARASAAC GitHub organization has a repository named `exhibit_images` described as a \"Test for new Arasaac API for images,\" indicating ongoing API development for image access[4].\n*   Discussions on GitHub issues also refer to \"ARASAAC told us about their API\" when integrating symbol search features into other applications[5].\n\nThe ARASAAC portal itself offers graphic resources and materials, and the symbol file libraries are available in PNG format[6]. Users can download individual pictograms directly from the website, which are provided in a transparent format[7]. However, for programmatic access, the API appears to be the intended method.\n\nTo find the specific API domain or documentation, further exploration of the ARASAAC website or their official GitHub resources related to their API would be necessary.\n\nSources:\n[1] [arasaac.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHSBcTSARwGfSbRbAyiOtzv8Uyms-bqEIaH_Xs3u55fmzBdh7RHc5F9T5EFjRmAIDGtKRIHs_11Hn5QBJUvbsSPEYX_eqFZWeuPF6Ec80qyI6mdTvg4vPvkoX3qO3HAFpFO0OV3RceonhPpXGGqCFM=)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGumgQmrlPw9RYJfy5j2cHgsPIWw2vLKqcfbFjWSwv9SP5D5r2kWuKXS5hIC-it0Ipz7JzIm3Y7I18we6CUwcfLBvsio8eDHdnAulwNLAfGrxYwEGOJWs-BTTBfpsHhlqOFKMPu)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEcvbZSqkUC7mJ57XxeSXYjp6NnroQ243srDGNymH0ibFVuZv2cLj7qovKrBF77roq9XpYsCLF4BhFmthyNbFAb19zRhkOAso36Yh7B7ztNIHwAuAVV-X7LtXx3j4WIoWk=)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQED8voktShO1M8tRupkocX7WYFH5Fo8rQKfZG8vUIkU4f-_CFwCkGReePhVY4KGsGQlS1dZfEzxYxv3odZ9j_cFri7rEsn7Odvk-RcJpHN861ZrbJvo)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFlrvUMUe469USuiJq8XtXAGSd8HgxI6Kcj2HqnXuOx0QmCE94DtyEVDvFswcJHItGxaBAGIptFEoyUz2y6qDenWVcFQKs1PXQ9QrI0rUquWfYXFVFk-qcQXAObdHpDoFFkQVnFkvU_aCe2NwQapA==)\n[6] [openassistive.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFNxwWkpjo-GZ0ZbhM8uMPQxpYPm_GFSS-g6PeX4Fkwus0AdwOTyNwEm-8nGz41EMcOSOKz5-ZUYHtx8rUax8c4leBSE-v8bJzG-SHQOv3cyAAjg71zz53wxcFK_Uvmg982BZKOWccmr8W0SJU=)\n[7] [arasaac.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHHeifdy_FJpYxXAhtkDspyYtxfch_pLzsCzSYPw_8MVyVvPB_JGwRLh5LgIxRh8zadhoJRg7WBq6BQYkoqtYOVFBiYHMg9Xpjrq2Bba_bHUsasPrVyqS5Ms6qpnUyTmful1fxo9LsKQD5HkBIuqQo1Kh4dHZXo-kBzrzb598bzudajwFlST6nABexpK-4D5lK0IEnQdg==)"
