steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1784727836
      nanos: 845287077
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Role: You are a Lead JavaScript Engineer specialising in Accessibility (AAC) and working with the ARASAC API.\n\nTask: Fix and refactor the pictogram fetching logic in my AAC Single-Page Web Application to eliminate incorrect image matches, broken links, and 404 errors when mapping Polish words to ARASAC pictograms.\n\nContext & Identified Issues:\n1. ARASAC API searches require base forms / infinitives in Polish (e.g., \"chcie\304\207\" instead of \"chc\304\231\", \"je\305\233\304\207\" instead of \"jem\"). Direct text matching for conjugated words fails.\n2. The search API endpoint (`/v1/pictograms/pl/search/{query}`) returns an array of objects. Selecting index 0 directly often yields wrong or obscure pictogram meanings.\n3. Polish diacritics (e.g., \304\205, \304\231, \304\207, \305\202, \305\233) are breaking `fetch()` requests if not properly URL-encoded.\n4. Static Core Vocabulary shouldn\'t rely on live search queries because API responses for basic words like \"ja\", \"to\", \"nie\" can be unpredictable.\n\nRequired Implementation Guidelines:\n\n1. Static Hardcoded Map for Core Vocabulary (S\305\202ownictwo Rdzenne):\n   - Replace API queries for Core Vocabulary with a static mapping array using proven, verified ARASAC Pictogram IDs:\n     - \"ja\": ID 5529\n     - \"chc\304\231\" / \"chcie\304\207\": ID 2445\n     - \"nie\": ID 5537\n     - \"to\": ID 36329\n     - \"lubi\304\231\" / \"lubi\304\207\": ID 3262\n     - \"stop\": ID 6242\n     - \"wi\304\231cej\": ID 7088\n     - \"gdzie\": ID 6231\n     - \"pomoc\": ID 5519\n     - \"koniec\": ID 6994\n   - Construct image URLs using: `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/{id}/{id}_500.png`\n\n2. Robust Helper Function for Dynamic Searches (Context Panel):\n   - Create a function `async function fetchPictogramUrl(searchTerm, fallbackLabel)` that:\n     a) Normalizes and URL-encodes the `searchTerm` using `encodeURIComponent()`.\n     b) Fetches from `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/pl/search/${encodedTerm}`.\n     c) Safely handles empty arrays or failed HTTP requests.\n     d) Extracts the correct `_id` from the response array and returns the proper image URL.\n     e) Implements a visual fallback (e.g., a stylized text-card or default icon) if no pictogram is found.\n\n3. Updated UI Logic:\n   - Ensure every pictogram card clearly displays its intended display label (in Polish, e.g., \"chc\304\231\") under the image, regardless of whether the internal search term was converted to its infinitive form (\"chcie\304\207\").\n\nOutput Format:\n- Provide the complete, updated HTML/JavaScript code for the Single-Page Application with these fixes integrated.\n- Briefly list the key changes made in the code to fix the pictogram matching issue."
    items {
      text: "Role: You are a Lead JavaScript Engineer specialising in Accessibility (AAC) and working with the ARASAC API.\n\nTask: Fix and refactor the pictogram fetching logic in my AAC Single-Page Web Application to eliminate incorrect image matches, broken links, and 404 errors when mapping Polish words to ARASAC pictograms.\n\nContext & Identified Issues:\n1. ARASAC API searches require base forms / infinitives in Polish (e.g., \"chcie\304\207\" instead of \"chc\304\231\", \"je\305\233\304\207\" instead of \"jem\"). Direct text matching for conjugated words fails.\n2. The search API endpoint (`/v1/pictograms/pl/search/{query}`) returns an array of objects. Selecting index 0 directly often yields wrong or obscure pictogram meanings.\n3. Polish diacritics (e.g., \304\205, \304\231, \304\207, \305\202, \305\233) are breaking `fetch()` requests if not properly URL-encoded.\n4. Static Core Vocabulary shouldn\'t rely on live search queries because API responses for basic words like \"ja\", \"to\", \"nie\" can be unpredictable.\n\nRequired Implementation Guidelines:\n\n1. Static Hardcoded Map for Core Vocabulary (S\305\202ownictwo Rdzenne):\n   - Replace API queries for Core Vocabulary with a static mapping array using proven, verified ARASAC Pictogram IDs:\n     - \"ja\": ID 5529\n     - \"chc\304\231\" / \"chcie\304\207\": ID 2445\n     - \"nie\": ID 5537\n     - \"to\": ID 36329\n     - \"lubi\304\231\" / \"lubi\304\207\": ID 3262\n     - \"stop\": ID 6242\n     - \"wi\304\231cej\": ID 7088\n     - \"gdzie\": ID 6231\n     - \"pomoc\": ID 5519\n     - \"koniec\": ID 6994\n   - Construct image URLs using: `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/{id}/{id}_500.png`\n\n2. Robust Helper Function for Dynamic Searches (Context Panel):\n   - Create a function `async function fetchPictogramUrl(searchTerm, fallbackLabel)` that:\n     a) Normalizes and URL-encodes the `searchTerm` using `encodeURIComponent()`.\n     b) Fetches from `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/pl/search/${encodedTerm}`.\n     c) Safely handles empty arrays or failed HTTP requests.\n     d) Extracts the correct `_id` from the response array and returns the proper image URL.\n     e) Implements a visual fallback (e.g., a stylized text-card or default icon) if no pictogram is found.\n\n3. Updated UI Logic:\n   - Ensure every pictogram card clearly displays its intended display label (in Polish, e.g., \"chc\304\231\") under the image, regardless of whether the internal search term was converted to its infinitive form (\"chcie\304\207\").\n\nOutput Format:\n- Provide the complete, updated HTML/JavaScript code for the Single-Page Application with these fixes integrated.\n- Briefly list the key changes made in the code to fix the pictogram matching issue."
    }
  }
}
