  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating API Structure**\n\nI\'m currently examining the structure of `STATIC_CORE_MAP` and `CORE_PICTOGRAMS_MAP` within `src/services/arasacApi.ts`. I\'m specifically looking at how these maps correlate Polish AAC vocabulary with ARASAC Pictogram IDs, and trying to bypass the API, which might be critical.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Core Word Mapping**\n\nI\'m now focusing on 100% reliability and speed, specifically for core words. I\'ve compiled a reliable, performant map of the core words that must bypass the API. I\'m prioritizing direct mapping of these essential terms. I\'m also looking at a dictionary of Polish verbs for dynamic searches.\n\n\n**Refining Lemma Handling**\n\nI\'m now integrating a list of verb conjugations to base forms (lemmas) directly into the lookup process. I\'ve built a function to normalize and search for lemmas such as `lubi` and `lubisz` to map onto `lubi\304\207`, and I\'m integrating this into `fetchPictogramUrl`, the core logic of the API.\n\n\n**Optimizing Core Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the `fetchPictogramUrl` function, prioritizing a static core map lookup first. If that fails, I\'m checking a lemma map for conjugated forms. Finally, I\'m making the API call as a last resort, which should reduce API queries. I\'m also adding logic to select the best ARASAC match.\n\n\n**Analyzing ARASAC Search Logic**\n\nI\'m now investigating `searchArasacPictograms` in `arasacApi.ts`. I\'m focusing on how it handles queries, caching, and API calls. I\'m examining the logic for trimming and lowercasing the query, checking the cache, and handling the `POLISH_LEMMA_MAP`. I\'m also looking into how it constructs the API URL and how it handles potential errors during the `fetch` operation.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 608726202
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
