  user_input {
    user_response: "Role: You are a Perfectionist QA Engineer and Senior Accessibility (AAC) Web Developer.\n\nGoal: Refactor the AAC Single-Page Web Application to GUARANTEE 100% reliable pictogram rendering without broken images, mismatched meanings, or CORS issues.\n\nCRITICAL FIXES TO IMPLEMENT:\n\n1. Vector SVG Standard & Anti-CORS:\n   - Use SVG format instead of PNG for all ARASAC assets.\n   - Base URL structure MUST be: `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/{id}/{id}.svg`\n\n2. Accurate Keyword Matching Algorithm (Fix Wrong Images):\n   - When calling `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/pl/search/{query}`, DO NOT blindly take `response[0]`.\n   - Iterate through the returned array and find the object where `keywords` contains an exact or closest match for the queried word. \n   - Fallback to `response[0]._id` ONLY if no exact match is found.\n\n3. Core Vocabulary Hardcoded Map (Verified SVG IDs):\n   - Strictly map static Core Vocabulary to these verified IDs:\n     * \"ja\": 5529\n     * \"chc\304\231\": 2445\n     * \"nie\": 5537\n     * \"to\": 36329\n     * \"lubi\304\231\": 3262\n     * \"stop\": 6242\n     * \"wi\304\231cej\": 7088\n     * \"gdzie\": 6231\n     * \"pomoc\": 5519\n     * \"koniec\": 6994\n\n4. Fail-Safe UI & Broken Image Handling (Graceful Degradation):\n   - Add an `onerror` inline handler to every `<img>` tag: `onerror=\"this.onerror=null; this.src=\'data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg...>[Text Fallback]</svg>\';\"`\n   - If an API fetch fails or returns empty `[]`, render a stylized text-card with the label instead of leaving a blank/broken image.\n   - Always wrap API fetches in `try/catch` blocks.\n\n5. URL Encoding:\n   - Always run search terms through `encodeURIComponent(term.toLowerCase().trim())`.\n\nOutput Requirements:\nProvide the full, production-ready, single-file HTML/JS/Tailwind code with zero console errors and full fallback UI handling."
    items {
      text: "Role: You are a Perfectionist QA Engineer and Senior Accessibility (AAC) Web Developer.\n\nGoal: Refactor the AAC Single-Page Web Application to GUARANTEE 100% reliable pictogram rendering without broken images, mismatched meanings, or CORS issues.\n\nCRITICAL FIXES TO IMPLEMENT:\n\n1. Vector SVG Standard & Anti-CORS:\n   - Use SVG format instead of PNG for all ARASAC assets.\n   - Base URL structure MUST be: `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/{id}/{id}.svg`\n\n2. Accurate Keyword Matching Algorithm (Fix Wrong Images):\n   - When calling `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/pl/search/{query}`, DO NOT blindly take `response[0]`.\n   - Iterate through the returned array and find the object where `keywords` contains an exact or closest match for the queried word. \n   - Fallback to `response[0]._id` ONLY if no exact match is found.\n\n3. Core Vocabulary Hardcoded Map (Verified SVG IDs):\n   - Strictly map static Core Vocabulary to these verified IDs:\n     * \"ja\": 5529\n     * \"chc\304\231\": 2445\n     * \"nie\": 5537\n     * \"to\": 36329\n     * \"lubi\304\231\": 3262\n     * \"stop\": 6242\n     * \"wi\304\231cej\": 7088\n     * \"gdzie\": 6231\n     * \"pomoc\": 5519\n     * \"koniec\": 6994\n\n4. Fail-Safe UI & Broken Image Handling (Graceful Degradation):\n   - Add an `onerror` inline handler to every `<img>` tag: `onerror=\"this.onerror=null; this.src=\'data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg...>[Text Fallback]</svg>\';\"`\n   - If an API fetch fails or returns empty `[]`, render a stylized text-card with the label instead of leaving a blank/broken image.\n   - Always wrap API fetches in `try/catch` blocks.\n\n5. URL Encoding:\n   - Always run search terms through `encodeURIComponent(term.toLowerCase().trim())`.\n\nOutput Requirements:\nProvide the full, production-ready, single-file HTML/JS/Tailwind code with zero console errors and full fallback UI handling."
    }
  }
}
