  user_input {
    user_response: "Role: You are a Senior Software Engineer specializing in NLP and Search Algorithms for Accessibility Apps.\n\nGoal: Fix the root cause of ARASAC API returning wrong pictograms (e.g., returning \"churros\" for \"lubi\304\231\" or \"peeling oranges\" for \"nie\"). Build a UNIVERSAL Smart Matcher module that works for ANY word requested dynamically.\n\nTHE PROBLEM WITH ARASAC API:\nCalling `GET /v1/pictograms/pl/search/{word}` returns an array of loose matches. The 0th element (`response[0]`) is almost always incorrect because ARASAC matches secondary tags and similar letter patterns.\n\nREQUIREMENTS FOR THE UNIVERSAL SEARCH ENGINE:\n\n1. Lemmatization & Dictionary Fallback Map:\n   Create a JS helper `normalizePolishWord(word)` that maps conjugated forms to infinitives/nominatives before querying:\n   - \"chc\304\231\", \"chcesz\", \"chce\" -> \"chcie\304\207\"\n   - \"lubi\304\231\", \"lubisz\" -> \"lubi\304\207\"\n   - \"jem\", \"jesz\" -> \"je\305\233\304\207\"\n   - \"pij\304\231\" -> \"pi\304\207\"\n   - \"id\304\231\" -> \"i\305\233\304\207\"\n\n2. Smart Result Parser Algorithm (`findBestPictogram(responseArray, searchedWord)`):\n   Instead of blindly taking `response[0]`, iterate through `responseArray`:\n   - Step A: Look for an item where `item.keywords` contains a keyword strictly equal to `searchedWord` AND `keyword.type === 1` (Primary Meaning). Return its `_id`.\n   - Step B: If Step A fails, look for an item where `item.keywords` contains `searchedWord` with any type.\n   - Step C: If still no exact match, fallback to the first item that has a category matching the context (e.g., \"verbs\" or \"actions\").\n   - Step D: If array is empty, return a Fail-Safe Styled Text Card (Do NOT display broken/unrelated images).\n\n3. Universal Dynamic Context Builder:\n   Allow adding ANY dynamic category (e.g., \"Owoce\", \"Zabawki\", \"Emocje\") using plain Polish word lists. The app must process all of them through the Smart Matcher asynchronously using `Promise.all()`.\n\nOutput Code Requirements:\nProvide a single-file HTML/JS app containing this robust Smart Matcher algorithm, ensuring no mismatched images ever appear regardless of what new vocabulary or context is added."
    items {
      text: "Role: You are a Senior Software Engineer specializing in NLP and Search Algorithms for Accessibility Apps.\n\nGoal: Fix the root cause of ARASAC API returning wrong pictograms (e.g., returning \"churros\" for \"lubi\304\231\" or \"peeling oranges\" for \"nie\"). Build a UNIVERSAL Smart Matcher module that works for ANY word requested dynamically.\n\nTHE PROBLEM WITH ARASAC API:\nCalling `GET /v1/pictograms/pl/search/{word}` returns an array of loose matches. The 0th element (`response[0]`) is almost always incorrect because ARASAC matches secondary tags and similar letter patterns.\n\nREQUIREMENTS FOR THE UNIVERSAL SEARCH ENGINE:\n\n1. Lemmatization & Dictionary Fallback Map:\n   Create a JS helper `normalizePolishWord(word)` that maps conjugated forms to infinitives/nominatives before querying:\n   - \"chc\304\231\", \"chcesz\", \"chce\" -> \"chcie\304\207\"\n   - \"lubi\304\231\", \"lubisz\" -> \"lubi\304\207\"\n   - \"jem\", \"jesz\" -> \"je\305\233\304\207\"\n   - \"pij\304\231\" -> \"pi\304\207\"\n   - \"id\304\231\" -> \"i\305\233\304\207\"\n\n2. Smart Result Parser Algorithm (`findBestPictogram(responseArray, searchedWord)`):\n   Instead of blindly taking `response[0]`, iterate through `responseArray`:\n   - Step A: Look for an item where `item.keywords` contains a keyword strictly equal to `searchedWord` AND `keyword.type === 1` (Primary Meaning). Return its `_id`.\n   - Step B: If Step A fails, look for an item where `item.keywords` contains `searchedWord` with any type.\n   - Step C: If still no exact match, fallback to the first item that has a category matching the context (e.g., \"verbs\" or \"actions\").\n   - Step D: If array is empty, return a Fail-Safe Styled Text Card (Do NOT display broken/unrelated images).\n\n3. Universal Dynamic Context Builder:\n   Allow adding ANY dynamic category (e.g., \"Owoce\", \"Zabawki\", \"Emocje\") using plain Polish word lists. The app must process all of them through the Smart Matcher asynchronously using `Promise.all()`.\n\nOutput Code Requirements:\nProvide a single-file HTML/JS app containing this robust Smart Matcher algorithm, ensuring no mismatched images ever appear regardless of what new vocabulary or context is added."
    }
  }
}
