    thinking: "**Analyzing Applet Compilation**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that both `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` completed successfully. I\'ve been reviewing the recent implementation, specifically the lemmatization and dictionary fallback mechanism (`normalizePolishWord` / `POLISH_LEMMA_MAP`), which successfully normalizes Polish verb and noun forms. I\'m focusing on its broader applicability.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have implemented the **Universal Smart Matcher Module** and ARASAC API parsing fixes across the AAC Application:\n\n### Core Architecture Improvements\n\n- **Lemmatization Dictionary (`normalizePolishWord`)**: Added mapping for conjugated Polish verbs and nouns to base infinitives and nominatives (e.g., `chc\304\231` $\\rightarrow$ `chcie\304\207`, `lubi\304\231` $\\rightarrow$ `lubi\304\207`, `jem` $\\rightarrow$ `je\305\233\304\207`, `id\304\231` $\\rightarrow$ `i\305\233\304\207`) prior to making network queries.\n- **Smart Result Parser (`findBestPictogram`)**:\n  - **Step A**: Filters for exact keyword matches with `type === 1` (Primary Meaning).\n  - **Step B**: Checks for exact keyword matches across any keyword type.\n  - **Step C**: Checks for substring matches within keyword arrays.\n  - **Step D**: Fallbacks safely to `response[0]` or triggers fail-safe text cards when no match exists.\n- **Static Core Vocabulary Mapping (`CORE_PICTOGRAMS_MAP`)**: Uses verified ARASAC Pictogram IDs (`ja`: 5529, `chc\304\231`: 2445, `nie`: 5537, `to`: 36329, `lubi\304\231`: 3262, `stop`: 6242, `wi\304\231cej`: 7088, `gdzie`: 6231, `pomoc`: 5519, `koniec`: 5358) for zero-latency loading of essential terms.\n- **Vector SVG Delivery & Fail-Safe Rendering**: Uses vector SVG URLs (`https://static.arasaac.org/pictograms/{id}/{id}.svg`) with PNG secondary fallback and inline SVG text card `onError` handlers to eliminate broken image icons."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 25130386
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
