    modified_response: "I have implemented the AAC Board Architecture, eliminating live search overhead from the main board rendering loop and standardizing vector SVG pictogram rendering:\n\n- **Local Vocabulary Database (`VOCABULARY_DB`)**: Structured static Polish core vocabulary (`CORE_VOCABULARY`) and context categories (`dom`, `szko\305\202a`, `park`, `jedzenie`, `emocje`, `miejsca`, `zabawa`, `zdrowie`) using verified static ARASAC IDs.\n- **Vector SVG & Resilient Fallbacks**:\n  - Configured `getArasacImageUrl` to load crisp, scalable vector SVG assets (`https://static.arasaac.org/pictograms/{id}/{id}.svg`).\n  - Implemented multi-stage fallback cascades (SVG $\\rightarrow$ PNG $\\rightarrow$ Styled letter-badge fallback) with inline `onError` handlers across `PictogramCard`, `SentenceBar`, and `FullScreenSentenceModal`.\n- **Smart Search & Lemmatization Engine**:\n  - Integrated `normalizePolishWord` for Polish verb/noun conjugation mapping (e.g. *chc\304\231* $\\rightarrow$ *chcie\304\207*, *lubi\304\231* $\\rightarrow$ *lubi\304\207*).\n  - Built `findBestPictogram` algorithm to evaluate primary keyword types and exact term matches prior to fallback.\n- **Fitzgerald Key Visual Hierarchy**:\n  - Applied color-coded categories (Yellow for pronouns/persons, Green for verbs, Red for negations/stop, Blue for social, Pink/Orange for nouns) with contrast borders and responsive touch targets."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 396309045
    }
