steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1784741742
      nanos: 453349392
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Role: You are a Senior Accessibility (AAC) Web Engineer and JavaScript Architect.\n\nGoal: Build a Single-Page Web Application for a Context-Adaptive AAC Board using ARASAC pictograms that natively solves the Polish translation matching bug.\n\nTHE ROOT CAUSE & ARCHITECTURAL SOLUTION:\nThe ARASAC Polish search API (`/pl/search/`) returns mismatched images because translation tags are auto-generated. However, the native Spanish API (`/es/search/`) is 100% accurate. \nTo fix this globally, implement a Polish-to-Spanish Translation Layer (PL -> ES) for API calls. The user will see Polish labels, but the background engine queries the Spanish API endpoint (`/v1/pictograms/es/search/{spanishTerm}`).\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\n1. Translation Layer & Dictionary Map (`PL_TO_ES_MAP`):\n   Create a comprehensive dictionary object in JS mapping Polish words to Spanish infinitives/base nouns:\n   - \"ja\" -> \"yo\"\n   - \"chc\304\231\" -> \"querer\"\n   - \"nie\" -> \"no\"\n   - \"lubi\304\231\" -> \"gustar\"\n   - \"stop\" -> \"parar\"\n   - \"wi\304\231cej\" -> \"m\303\241s\"\n   - \"gdzie\" -> \"d\303\263nde\"\n   - \"pomoc\" -> \"ayuda\"\n   - \"je\305\233\304\207\" -> \"comer\"\n   - \"pi\304\207\" -> \"beber\"\n   - \"spa\304\207\" -> \"dormir\"\n   - \"toaleta\" -> \"aseo\"\n   - \"k\304\205piel\" -> \"ba\303\261o\"\n   - \"mama\" -> \"mam\303\241\"\n   - \"pisa\304\207\" -> \"escribir\"\n   - \"czyta\304\207\" -> \"leer\"\n   - \"biega\304\207\" -> \"correr\"\n   - \"hu\305\233tawka\" -> \"columpio\"\n   - \"pies\" -> \"perro\"\n\n2. Async Smart Fetcher (`getPictogram(polishWord)`):\n   - Normalize input: convert to lowercase and look up in `PL_TO_ES_MAP`.\n   - If mapped, fetch from `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/es/search/${encodeURIComponent(spanishTerm)}`.\n   - Take `response[0]._id` and return image URL: `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/${id}/${id}_500.png`.\n   - Implement `try/catch` with a clean text-card fallback if fetching fails.\n\n3. Google AI Studio Sandbox Compatibility Rules:\n   - DO NOT use inline event handlers (e.g., `onclick=\"...\"` or `onchange=\"...\"`). They get blocked by AI Studio\'s iframe CSP.\n   - Dynamically attach all click/change event listeners using JS `addEventListener()` inside `document.addEventListener(\'DOMContentLoaded\', ...)`.\n\n4. Application Layout:\n   - Sentence Bar at the top (with \"Usu\305\204\", \"Wyczy\305\233\304\207\" buttons and dynamically appended cards).\n   - Core Vocabulary Grid (70% width) - always visible (\"Ja\", \"Chc\304\231\", \"Nie\", \"Lubi\304\231\", \"Stop\", \"Wi\304\231cej\").\n   - Dynamic Context Panel (30% width) - dropdown/buttons to switch contexts (\"Dom\", \"Szko\305\202a\", \"Park\").\n   - Category badges on cards (\"Osoby\", \"Czasowniki\", \"Przeczenie\") with distinct border colors.\n\nOutput:\nProvide the full, standalone, single-file HTML/JS/Tailwind CSS code ready for immediate Preview in Google AI Studio."
    items {
      text: "Role: You are a Senior Accessibility (AAC) Web Engineer and JavaScript Architect.\n\nGoal: Build a Single-Page Web Application for a Context-Adaptive AAC Board using ARASAC pictograms that natively solves the Polish translation matching bug.\n\nTHE ROOT CAUSE & ARCHITECTURAL SOLUTION:\nThe ARASAC Polish search API (`/pl/search/`) returns mismatched images because translation tags are auto-generated. However, the native Spanish API (`/es/search/`) is 100% accurate. \nTo fix this globally, implement a Polish-to-Spanish Translation Layer (PL -> ES) for API calls. The user will see Polish labels, but the background engine queries the Spanish API endpoint (`/v1/pictograms/es/search/{spanishTerm}`).\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\n1. Translation Layer & Dictionary Map (`PL_TO_ES_MAP`):\n   Create a comprehensive dictionary object in JS mapping Polish words to Spanish infinitives/base nouns:\n   - \"ja\" -> \"yo\"\n   - \"chc\304\231\" -> \"querer\"\n   - \"nie\" -> \"no\"\n   - \"lubi\304\231\" -> \"gustar\"\n   - \"stop\" -> \"parar\"\n   - \"wi\304\231cej\" -> \"m\303\241s\"\n   - \"gdzie\" -> \"d\303\263nde\"\n   - \"pomoc\" -> \"ayuda\"\n   - \"je\305\233\304\207\" -> \"comer\"\n   - \"pi\304\207\" -> \"beber\"\n   - \"spa\304\207\" -> \"dormir\"\n   - \"toaleta\" -> \"aseo\"\n   - \"k\304\205piel\" -> \"ba\303\261o\"\n   - \"mama\" -> \"mam\303\241\"\n   - \"pisa\304\207\" -> \"escribir\"\n   - \"czyta\304\207\" -> \"leer\"\n   - \"biega\304\207\" -> \"correr\"\n   - \"hu\305\233tawka\" -> \"columpio\"\n   - \"pies\" -> \"perro\"\n\n2. Async Smart Fetcher (`getPictogram(polishWord)`):\n   - Normalize input: convert to lowercase and look up in `PL_TO_ES_MAP`.\n   - If mapped, fetch from `https://api.arasac.org/v1/pictograms/es/search/${encodeURIComponent(spanishTerm)}`.\n   - Take `response[0]._id` and return image URL: `https://static.arasac.org/pictograms/${id}/${id}_500.png`.\n   - Implement `try/catch` with a clean text-card fallback if fetching fails.\n\n3. Google AI Studio Sandbox Compatibility Rules:\n   - DO NOT use inline event handlers (e.g., `onclick=\"...\"` or `onchange=\"...\"`). They get blocked by AI Studio\'s iframe CSP.\n   - Dynamically attach all click/change event listeners using JS `addEventListener()` inside `document.addEventListener(\'DOMContentLoaded\', ...)`.\n\n4. Application Layout:\n   - Sentence Bar at the top (with \"Usu\305\204\", \"Wyczy\305\233\304\207\" buttons and dynamically appended cards).\n   - Core Vocabulary Grid (70% width) - always visible (\"Ja\", \"Chc\304\231\", \"Nie\", \"Lubi\304\231\", \"Stop\", \"Wi\304\231cej\").\n   - Dynamic Context Panel (30% width) - dropdown/buttons to switch contexts (\"Dom\", \"Szko\305\202a\", \"Park\").\n   - Category badges on cards (\"Osoby\", \"Czasowniki\", \"Przeczenie\") with distinct border colors.\n\nOutput:\nProvide the full, standalone, single-file HTML/JS/Tailwind CSS code ready for immediate Preview in Google AI Studio."
    }
  }
}
