    thinking: "**Defining the Core Task**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the essence of the prompt: crafting a Polish-to-Spanish translation layer specifically for ARASAC API queries. The key focus is building a `PL_TO_ES_MAP` to translate Polish terms to Spanish infinitives or base nouns, aiming to minimize translation errors in dynamic API interactions with ARASAC.\n\n\n**Expanding the Translation Map**\n\nI\'m actively expanding the `PL_TO_ES_MAP` with common Polish words, now including terms like \"yo\" from \"ja,\" \"querer\" from \"chc\304\231,\" and \"no\" from \"nie.\" I am also adding words such as \"gustar,\" \"parar,\" \"m\303\241s,\" \"d\303\263nde,\" \"ayuda,\" \"comer,\" \"beber,\" \"dormir,\" \"aseo,\" \"ba\303\261o,\" \"mam\303\241,\" \"escribir,\" \"leer,\" \"correr,\" \"columpio,\" and \"perro\". This growing map will soon cover core phrases!\n\n\n**Mapping ARASAC API Queries**\n\nI\'m now incorporating API call specifics. Steps include mapping Polish terms, using `findBestPictogram`, and constructing the SVG URL from the chosen pictogram. This involves refining the process of translating Polish terms to Spanish, crucial for accurate ARASAC API interactions. I\'m focusing on the implementation details using the `PL_TO_ES_MAP`. I am now making the appropriate data calls based on the Spanish translation.\n\n\n**Analyzing API Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/services/arasacApi.ts` to examine how `fetchPictogramUrl` uses `PL_TO_ES_MAP` within the broader ARASAC API interactions. I\'ve pinpointed the key steps within `fetchPictogramUrl`, specifically how it trims, lowercases, consults caches, and leverages both `POLISH_LEMMA_MAP` and, importantly, `PL_TO_ES_MAP` to craft Spanish search queries for the ARASAC API. The tracing confirms its central role in facilitating the Polish-to-Spanish translation.\n\n```\n\n"
